# slow-light — pattern
@id slow-light  @kind pattern  @layer library  @author toine  @lang en

## summary
~ No clock. Time is only the light changing; the session ends when the carrier decides, never because a resource ran out. Use it instead of ticking-clock for a contemplative story.

## roles
role keeper : character : who feels the time passing
role wrap_line : line : what the keeper says when the scene has gone long

## params
param step = 1 : degrees of sun per minute
param steps = 12 : how many minutes the light keeps rising
param long_s = 900 : seconds after which the keeper starts to wrap up

## principles
~0.7 $keeper notices the light, not the time.

## rules
when clock.every(60) max $steps -> light.raise($step) {rise}
when time.elapsed($long_s) once if not ending.any -> say($wrap_line) {wrap}

## beats_hint
hint no ending can be forced by time; every ending must come from a decision

## variations
variation dusk : the light falls instead; same rules with a negative step
